{"book":"Mark","chapter":12,"translation":"KJV","url":"/bible/mark/12","verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"And he began to speak unto them by parables. A certain man planted a vineyard, and set an hedge about it, and digged a place for the winefat, and built a tower, and let it out to husbandmen, and went into a far country.","words":[["And",["G2532"]],["he began",["G756"]],["to speak",["G3004"]],["unto them",["G846"]],["by",["G1722"]],["parables.",["G3850"]],["A certain man",["G444"]],["planted",["G5452"]],["a vineyard,",["G290"]],["and",["G2532"]],["set",["G4060"]],["an hedge about",["G5418"]],["it, and",["G2532"]],["digged",["G3736"]],["a place for the winefat,",["G5276"]],["and",["G2532"]],["built",["G3618"]],["a tower,",["G4444"]],["and",["G2532"]],["let",["G1554"]],["it",["G846"]],["out",["G1554"]],["to husbandmen,",["G1092"]],["and",["G2532"]],["went into a far country.",[]]]},{"verse":2,"text":"And at the season he sent to the husbandmen a servant, that he might receive from the husbandmen of the fruit of the vineyard.","words":[["And",["G2532"]],["at the season",["G2540"]],["he sent",["G649"]],["to",["G4314"]],["the husbandmen",["G1092"]],["a servant,",["G1401"]],["that",["G2443"]],["he might receive",["G2983"]],["from",["G3844"]],["the husbandmen",["G1092"]],["of",["G575"]],["the fruit",["G2590"]],["of the vineyard.",[]]]},{"verse":3,"text":"And they caught him, and beat him, and sent him away empty.","words":[["And",["G1161"]],["they caught",["G2983"]],["him, and beat",["G1194"]],["him,",["G846"]],["and",["G2532"]],["sent him away",["G649"]],["empty.",[]]]},{"verse":4,"text":"And again he sent unto them another servant; and at him they cast stones, and wounded him in the head, and sent him away shamefully handled.","words":[["And",["G2532"]],["again",["G3825"]],["he sent",["G649"]],["unto",["G4314"]],["them",["G846"]],["another",["G243"]],["servant;",["G1401"]],["and at him",["G2548"]],["they cast stones,",["G3036"]],["and wounded him in the head,",["G2775"]],["and",["G2532"]],["sent him away",["G649"]],["shamefully handled.",[]]]},{"verse":5,"text":"And again he sent another; and him they killed, and many others; beating some, and killing some.","words":[["And",["G2532"]],["again",["G3825"]],["he sent",["G649"]],["another;",["G243"]],["and him",["G2548"]],["they killed,",["G615"]],["and",["G2532"]],["many",["G4183"]],["others;",["G243","G3303"]],["beating some,",["G1194"]],["and",["G1161"]],["killing some.",[]]]},{"verse":6,"text":"Having yet therefore one son, his wellbeloved, he sent him also last unto them, saying, They will reverence my son.","words":[["Having",["G2192"]],["yet",["G2089"]],["therefore",["G3767"]],["one",["G1520"]],["son,",["G5207"]],["his",["G846"]],["wellbeloved,",["G27"]],["he sent",["G649"]],["him",["G846"]],["also",["G2532"]],["last",["G2078"]],["unto",["G4314"]],["them,",["G846"]],["saying,",["G3004","G3754"]],["They will reverence",["G1788"]],["my",["G3450"]],["son.",[]]]},{"verse":7,"text":"But those husbandmen said among themselves, This is the heir; come, let us kill him, and the inheritance shall be ours.","words":[["But",["G1161"]],["those",["G1565"]],["husbandmen",["G1092"]],["said",["G2036"]],["among",["G4314"]],["themselves,",["G1438"]],["This",["G3754","G3778"]],["is",["G2076"]],["the heir;",["G2818"]],["come,",["G1205"]],["let us kill",["G615"]],["him,",["G846"]],["and",["G2532"]],["the inheritance",["G2817"]],["shall be",["G2071"]],["ours.",[]]]},{"verse":8,"text":"And they took him, and killed him, and cast him out of the vineyard.","words":[["And",["G2532"]],["they took",["G2983"]],["him,",["G846"]],["and killed",["G615"]],["him, and",["G2532"]],["cast",["G1544"]],["him out of",["G1854"]],["the vineyard.",[]]]},{"verse":9,"text":"What shall therefore the lord of the vineyard do? he will come and destroy the husbandmen, and will give the vineyard unto others.","words":[["What",["G5101"]],["shall",["G4160"]],["therefore",["G3767"]],["the lord",["G2962"]],["of the vineyard",["G290"]],[